DECISIONS 320, 323 (CODEGEN.md §2.8, §5.14): checks and builds, its Go vetting and its C++ and TypeScript compiling; formerly E8019_96, refused: CODEGEN.md §5.9, §7.3: a baked cpp emit fills every value inside detail::<P>Access::Build, the friend of its own package's classes only, so a value holding a record of another package is refused.
-- b/b.canon --
package b

/// A point.
record Point {
  /// Across.
  x: Int
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/b", namespace: "b", mode: baked }
-- a/a.canon --
package a

import b { Point }

/// The corner.
let corner: Point = { x: 1 }

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: baked }
-- a.corner.json --
{"x": 1}
-- findings.txt --
0 errors, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
